# Force LF line endings on checkout regardless of platform or local git
# config. Without this, Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf=true, the default
# on GitHub's windows-latest runners and many Windows git installs) convert
# these to CRLF, which breaks the generated-adapter drift check — the
# generator always writes LF, so a CRLF file on disk looks like drift that
# isn't real. See wiki/gotchas (private) for the incident this fixes.
* text=auto eol=lf
